      "answer": {
        "lead": "You can carry over up to 5 unused PTO days into next year. Any days above that are forfeited on December 31.",
        "policy_facts": [
          {
            "text": "The standard cap is 5 unused PTO days carried into the next calendar year. Unused days above the cap are forfeited on December 31.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "5.1",
                "snippet": "You can carry over up to 5 unused PTO days into the next calendar year."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Forfeited days are not paid out. Carried-over days appear in your balance on January 1 and are used like any other PTO.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "5.1",
                "snippet": "Forfeited days are not paid out."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "If you are on approved leave that spans December 31, such as parental leave, the cap is 10 days instead of 5. It is applied automatically.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "5.2",
                "snippet": "If you are on approved leave that spans December 31, you can carry over up to 10 unused PTO days instead of 5."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "As of 2026-11-02 you have 11.0 PTO days available. That is 16.67 accrued plus 2.0 carried over, minus 7.67 used, with 0.0 pending.",
            "citations": [],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "check_pto_balance"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "recommendations": [
          {
            "text": "If you took no more PTO and accrued nothing further, you would be about 6 days over the 5-day cap. Plan to use those days before December 31."
          },
          {
            "text": "Check your expected carryover in the HR Portal, which shows it from autumn onwards."
          },
          {
            "text": "I can check specific dates against your balance and draft a request to your manager, Jordan Lee, if you'd like."
          }
        ]
      },
